      "end": 69.17,
      "duration": 68.64,
      "text": "Distinguished colleagues, UNESCO partners, champions of universal information access. As we gather to celebrate the international day of for universal access to information, we face a key moment in this age, the digital age, today marks the sixth AI for information access conference building on years of crucial dialogue about how artificial intelligence can serve information accessibility, not as an abstract philosophical technological possibility, but as a fundamental human rights that demands immediate coordinated action. Speaking from my experience working at the European Union level, I want to share how policy frameworks, public-private partnerships, strategic regulation can transform artificial intelligence from a potential barrier into a powerful enabler of information accessibility for all. The European Union has positioned itself at the forefront of responsible AI governance,",
