      "text": "markets. The business case is before us. It's compelling. It requires, however, policy frameworks and architectures that reward long-term inclusive innovation over shortened profit maximization. One area where European experience offers particularly valuable lessons and we will discuss it right now is multilingual AI development, the EU commitment to linguistic diversity with 24 official languages and hundreds of regional languages has forced the European Union to confront AI's monolingable bias head-on. Investments at your level in multilingual AI research through programmes like Horizon Europe and the digital Europe programme demonstrate linguistic inclusions is not just possible technologically, but it's essential and it's a fundamental part in AI legitimacy. When AI systems can operate effectively in mouthies, Irish Gaelic, original languages",
