      "duration": 64.98,
      "text": "like Catalan or Welsh, they provide that the technological sophistication and cultural preservation can advance together. This European approach offers a model for global AI development rather than accepting English language as inevitable or dominant. We can invest in AI systems that truly serve global linguistic diversity. The window of shaping AI development around accessibility principles is rapidly closing. As AI systems become more entrenched, retro-freezing accessibility becomes more difficult and expensive. I would say we have five years probably to embed accessibility into AI foundational architecture. After that, we'll spend decades so much more time trying to fix systems designed without inclusion in mind. This is why events like today AI for the conference are so crucial and thank you for this opportunity.",
